course: dictionary
lesson: 12732
title: Saying things drily
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Drily tells you how someone says something. When a person makes a joke in a calm, serious voice, with a straight face, they speak drily. «"Nice weather for a picnic," said Mum drily, looking at the grey rain outside.» Her words sound serious, but the rain shows that she is joking.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Is the speaker being funny while looking serious? Does the sentence describe a calm face or a quiet voice? «He remarked drily that the homework was "a little bit easy".» The word drily warns you that he is teasing, not praising.
explain: Drily can also mean in a dry way, without water or wetness, but this is rare. In stories, it almost always means the funny, straight-faced way. Use the sentence to check which meaning fits.
fact: Drily is an adverb: it tells you how someone does something.
fact: «Drily» means in a funny way that seems serious, with a straight face.
fact: Dry humour is a joke said calmly, without a big smile or a laugh.
fact: The rare meaning of «drily» is in a dry way, without water or wetness.
exercise: «"We are having soup for dinner again," said Ben drily.» How did Ben say it? | Quickly, as he ran out of the room | Sadly, with tears in his eyes | Crossly and loudly | *With a straight face, as a dry joke
exercise: «She remarked drily that the test was "a walk in the park", when it had been very hard.» Why is this funny? | She is crying about the test | The test really was a walk in the park | She is singing a happy song | *She is joking in a serious voice, because the test was not easy
exercise: Which word tells you how Sam spoke? «Sam said drily, "Your shoelaces are very tidy today."» | today | said | shoelaces | *drily
test: «"Lovely, another puddle," muttered Gran drily as she stepped in one.» What does drily mean here? | *In a dry, straight-faced way, as a joke | Quickly, running away | In a loud, excited way | In a wet way, like the puddle
test: Which sentence uses drily correctly? | He drily laughed and cried at the film. | *"You've painted the whole kitchen, and you call that tidy," said Dad drily. | The towel was drily after the swim. | Drily, the sun came out and the rain fell.
exam: Read: «"I'm so glad we walked in the rain," said Lily drily.» What does drily tell you about Lily? | She is cross with the rain | *She is joking in a calm, straight-faced way | She is lost in the rain | She is singing happily in the rain
